{
  "about": "H3 model registry (Q-D14). Each logical model lists candidate builds in order of preference; the H3 serving check (E08-R008, analysis/e08/serving_check.py) tries them on a Kaggle T4 and the first that passes is pinned in configs/llm/pins.json (Hugging Face commit sha, vLLM version). T4 has no bf16, so dtype is half (fp16) or float32. 7-9B models are 4-bit so that two models (target + auditor) fit on 2 x T4, one per GPU.",
  "vllm_version": "0.19.1",
  "vllm_note": "0.19.1 is the newest vLLM on PyPI built on torch 2.10 / CUDA 12.8, the CUDA line Kaggle ships (its image has torch 2.11.0+cu128). vLLM >= 0.20 needs torch built on CUDA 13 and an NVIDIA driver >= 580. Correction after E08-R008: Kaggle's driver is 580.178, so CUDA 13 builds would load too; 0.19.1 is kept for the re-run so only the known failure causes change.",
  "attention_backend": "TRITON_ATTN",
  "attention_note": "E08-R008: on a T4 (sm75) vLLM 0.19.1 picks FlashInfer, which JIT-compiles kernels and fails to link on Kaggle; Triton attention needs no compile step.",
